{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAYm4psxQhz4wMTzWUGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BY6GCFyA5bJCL8KDnRDvGT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > $TMPDIR/draft.json <<'EOF'\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"F1\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/reports/closeout-read-view-federated-corpus.json\",\"line\":73,\"summary\":\"The R3 measurement report names the Harne8 and pose-dist pins but not the engine revision or binary digest that produced it ('built in isolated clone'). So the manual R3 evidence cannot be tied to the reviewed implementation (14aefb96/83334d02) or re-run by a reviewer.\",\"action\":\"Record the engine commit and binary digest, plus the exact command, in the federated-corpus report on its next regeneration\",\"owner\":\"role:maintainer\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-18\"},\n{\"id\":\"F2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\",\"line\":378,\"summary\":\"The amendment describes the 50,000 value as the 'shared capture and audit limit'. The same constant also bounds proof replay (governance_read_view.go:2410-2470) and the index-generation traversal preflight (index_generation.go:1080), and that traversal bound now rises too without being stated.\",\"action\":\"State in the ADR that proof replay and the index traversal preflight share the observation constant\",\"owner\":\"role:maintainer\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-18\"}\n],\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Verified: a single constant (governance_read_view.go:24) governs capture (630, 784-803), audit (180, 197) and proof replay (2131, 2410-2470). The byte, streamed and metadata limits are unchanged (16 MiB, 512 MiB, stream.go:27 8 GiB). An overlay mutation back to 40,000 fails TestGovernanceReadViewObservationLimit at record 40001, and the two-root test stays relative to the constant. Unresolved assumption: the Harne8 measurements of 41,128-41,208 observations (R3) are manual and were not reproducible here because the corpus is absent (F1). Accepted risk (D1 consequences): future corpus growth is not certified.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Only a constant changes. reserveRecord still takes budgetMu. go test -race on GovernanceReadView|ReviewOperationView|IndexFederatedMaterial passed locally.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\"rationale\":\"read_view schema_version and parser version are unchanged. Only the documented capacity number changes, in all four POSE.md copies.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Overflow still returns errGovernanceReadViewBudget and keeps its audit cause (integration_test.go:712-723). The new test proves refusal of the next record and that the metadata bound still applies.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The cross-root shared budget is preserved: each root fits alone and their total is refused (integration_test.go:699-723).\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The aggregate overflow audit cause is still asserted. No new logging was added and none is needed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"I checked POSE.md:385, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:389 and both scaffold copies; all agree on 50,000. Raising a cap only admits more operations; overflow semantics are unchanged.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The targeted race tests pass locally, and the boundary tests at 50,000/50,001 pass. Under the 40,000 mutation the test fails as expected.\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-295cfa7490dc68de\",\"rationale\":\"The measured 41,143 observations exceed 40,000 during federated material verification. Raising the shared cap (D1) addresses that cause directly while keeping tree comparison and federated bindings in one operation. pose assess design reproduced input digest 295cfa74 with one governance-contract delta.\",\"mappings\":[{\"delta\":\"SD-2d7579b1\",\"basis\":\"D1\",\"disposition\":\"mapped\",\"rationale\":\"D1 records the recalibration to 50,000 in this ADR; the amendment at lines 376-393 is that record.\"}]},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"All four doc copies and the ADR match the runtime constant. A minor scope omission is noted in F2 (low, accepted).\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Overflow still leaves freshness unknown with a budget cause. No remediation text changed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"R1: TestGovernanceReadViewObservationLimit, the probe capacity test and the directory-entry accounting through reserveDirectory. R2: the overflow refusal and metadata tests. R3: manual report showing three plans current with empty limitations (see F1).\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-295cfa7490dc68de\",\"rationale\":\"The diff matches the declared artifacts plus the index and validation bindings. Review policy, Harne8 pin and spec discovery are untouched (non-goals).\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Unknown inputs are still blocked. The cap stays bounded: memory growth of up to 10k records is constrained by the unchanged byte and metadata limits. No path or authority changes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-295cfa7490dc68de\",\"rationale\":\"This is the smallest sufficient change: one constant, with roughly 21% headroom over the measured 41,208. The alternative of scoping out the tree comparison or the federated checks was rejected because it removes evidence. No speculative extensibility. The choice is invalidated when the corpus exceeds about 50k observations, as the ADR acknowledges.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-read-view-covers-the-federated-corpus --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0. 9 claims and 14 observed paths; the 982 findings are repo-wide orphan warnings outside this scope.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-295cfa7490dc68de\",\"rationale\":\"Reproduced input digest sha256:295cfa74...\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Could not save .pose/state/components/pose-mcp.json because the review worktree is a read-only file system. Environmental; no assessment output was used.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"not-used\",\"rationale\":\"Attempted, but the save of .pose/state/integrations.json was refused on the read-only review worktree, so it produced no assessment. Integration was judged from sealed integration evidence.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt\",\"rationale\":\"Could not save .pose/state/technical-debt.json because the review worktree is a read-only file system. Environmental.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Its precondition is the recorded completion of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Its precondition is the attestation of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0. Rules for security, documentation-style and backend-go were considered.\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\",\"rationale\":\"Local run: 1 target, 233 results, 0 findings, exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\"rationale\":\"Sealed evidence is green and bound to git_head 83334d02; pose-mcp is unchanged up to d0d9980c. My sandboxed re-run exited 1 with 224/236 steps passing, 11 failures and 1 timeout, all in runtime, delegate, journey and chmod tests. Those failures reproduce identically with the base 40,000 limit overlaid, so they are environmental and not caused by this change. governance-read-view-integration passed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the workspace run: local strict module run gave 221/233 passing with the same 11 environmental failures and 1 timeout, which are invariant under the base-limit overlay. The sealed module evidence passes.\"}\n]}\nEOF\npython3 -I -c 'import json,sys;d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1]));print(\"ok\",len(d[\"criteria\"]),len(d[\"tools\"]),len(d[\"findings\"]))' $TMPDIR/draft.json","description":"Write and validate draft JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":68362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"476cd5f9-2ce2-477d-9afc-7ec64f23b1f8","timestamp":"2026-11-18T14:27:05.902Z","request_id":"req_011ChAYm4exLCDwFL34PcxWS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BY6GCFyA5bJCL8KDnRDvGT":{"command":"cat > $TMPDIR/draft.json <<'EOF'\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"F1\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/reports/closeout-read-view-federated-corpus.json\",\"line\":73,\"summary\":\"The R3 measurement report names the Harne8 and pose-dist pins but not the engine revision or binary digest that produced it ('built in isolated clone'). So the manual R3 evidence cannot be tied to the reviewed implementation (14aefb96/83334d02) or re-run by a reviewer.\",\"action\":\"Record the engine commit and binary digest, plus the exact command, in the federated-corpus report on its next regeneration\",\"owner\":\"role:maintainer\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-18\"},\n{\"id\":\"F2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\",\"line\":378,\"summary\":\"The amendment describes the 50,000 value as the 'shared capture and audit limit'. The same constant also bounds proof replay (governance_read_view.go