n but couldn't save their output, because the review worktree is read-only.\n- **Docs:** `POSE.md`, the pt-BR copy and both scaffold copies all say 50,000.\n- **Committed validation:** `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json` is bound to `git_head` `83334d02`.\n\n## Criteria\nAll 15 are **passed**. The evidence and reasons are in the block below.\n\n## Structural fact\n- SD-2d7579b1 (ADR amendment) → **D1**, the decision to recalibrate the limit to 50,000 in that ADR.\n\n## Defects\n| id | severity | file:line | summary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | low | `.pose/reports/closeout-read-view-federated-corpus.json:73` | The R3 report doesn't name the engine commit or binary that produced it, so the manual evidence can't be tied to the reviewed code. I couldn't re-run it either, because the Harne8 corpus isn't available here. |\n| F2 | low | `.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md:378` | The amendment calls 50,000 the \"capture and audit\" limit. It doesn't mention that proof replay and the index traversal check share the same constant, so that traversal bound also went up. |\n\nBoth are follow-ups with an action, owner and review date, so they are accepted as low risks.\n\n## Cleanup\nI waited for all test, build and background jobs to finish. As the final command, inside the sandbox, I ran `go clean -cache` and removed the leftover `go-build*` directories under `$GOTMPDIR`. Both succeeded, and none remain.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"F1\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/reports/closeout-read-view-federated-corpus.json\",\"line\":73,\"summary\":\"The R3 measurement report names the Harne8 and pose-dist pins but not the engine revision or binary digest that produced it ('built in isolated clone'). So the manual R3 evidence cannot be tied to the reviewed implementation (14aefb96/83334d02) or re-run by a reviewer.\",\"acti